---
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/schema';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — BVT';
const description =
  'How BVT handles public page data, extension storage, TikTok requests, Pro license validation, and this static website.';
const gaEnabled = Boolean(SITE.gaMeasurementId);
const lastUpdated = 'November 15, 2026';
const jsonLd = [
  breadcrumbSchema([
    { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
    { name: 'Privacy', href: '/privacy/' },
  ]),
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/privacy/" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <section class="border-b border-slate-200 bg-slate-50">
    <div class="container-page py-10 sm:py-14">
      <Breadcrumbs
        items={[
          { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
          { name: 'Privacy', href: '/privacy/' },
        ]}
      />
      <div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl">
        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-brand-600">
          Legal &amp; privacy
        </p>
        <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-5xl">
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">
          This policy describes the BVT Chrome extension and this website. It is written
          to match the current build, including what the extension does{' '}
          <strong>not</strong> do.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container-page py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="prose max-w-3xl">
      <div class="not-prose mb-10 rounded-2xl border border-brand-200 bg-brand-50/70 p-5 text-sm leading-6 text-brand-950">
        <div class="flex gap-3">
          <Icon name="shield" class="mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-brand-700" />
          <p>
            <strong>Short version:</strong> BVT processes public page data in your browser.
            It does not upload page data to BVT servers. Downloads request media from
            TikTok’s domains when you start them. Pro validation contacts the license
            server at <code>pandahi.cc</code> with an account identifier and token, not page
            data. The extension contains no analytics or telemetry.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>1. Scope</h2>
      <p>
        This policy covers the BVT browser extension and the public website at{' '}
        <a href={SITE.url}>{SITE.url}</a>. It does not cover TikTok, the Chrome Web Store,
        the payment processor, or any other third-party service you choose to use. Those
        services have their own policies.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What the extension reads</h2>
      <p>
        BVT is built for public TikTok pages you open. Depending on the page, it reads
        information already present in the page: rendered video cards, read-only React
        props exposed by the page, and embedded page JSON. The fields can include video
        IDs, descriptions, covers, counts, author identifiers, playlist context, video
        sources, and short drama episode data.
      </p>
      <p>
        BVT does not bypass login, CAPTCHA, region restrictions, DRM, or rate limits. It
        is intended for public pages. It does not collect private messages, passwords, or
        content that the page does not make available.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Where page data is processed</h2>
      <p>
        Page data is processed locally in your browser. BVT does not upload page data to a
        BVT server. It does not sell page data or use it for advertising. It does not run a
        background crawler or build a hidden library of videos.
      </p>
      <p>
        Settings, filename preferences, a small profile <code>secUid</code> cache, and an
        encrypted Pro credential can be stored in <code>chrome.storage.local</code>. Page
        content used by the panels is kept in the page context and is not sent to BVT.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Network requests</h2>
      <p>
        Network activity falls into four narrow categories. They are separate from page
        data collection.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Page data for the page you opened.</strong> When you start a creator or
          short drama workflow, BVT requests TikTok’s own public endpoints for that page to
          load additional posts or episodes. The request is tied to the page you are on
          and the action you started.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Downloads.</strong> When you click a download control, BVT requests the
          media URL from TikTok’s media domains and writes the file locally. The request is
          user-initiated.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Pro license validation.</strong> When you open the subscription flow,
          restore a license, refresh status, or trigger a paid feature while a check is
          required, the extension contacts <code>pandahi.cc</code>. The request can include
          an account identifier, token, channel, and operation type. It does{' '}
          <strong>not</strong> include page data or downloaded media.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Support links.</strong> Email support opens your mail client. BVT does not
          include a contact form and does not read your email.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Permissions</h2>
      <p>The current extension manifest requests:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <code>storage</code> — settings, filename preferences, download counts, the
          profile <code>secUid</code> cache, and the Pro credential.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>tabs</code> — opening the subscription page and sending streamed download
          chunks to the active tab.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>webRequest</code> — observing TikTok’s post-list response so the extension
          can associate a public profile with its <code>secUid</code> for creator
          workflows. The extension does not store media responses.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>declarativeNetRequest</code> — setting Referer, Origin, and CORS headers on
          user-initiated TikTok media requests so the download can complete in the browser.
        </li>
        <li>
          Host permissions for <code>*.tiktok.com</code> and <code>*.tiktokcdn.com</code> —
          the public page script and user-initiated media requests.
        </li>
        <li>
          Host permission for <code>pandahi.cc</code> — Pro activation, license restore, and
          status refresh.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        BVT does not request <code>&lt;all_urls&gt;</code>, the Chrome <code>downloads</code>{' '}
        permission, the camera, the microphone, or your location.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Local storage and retention</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Settings and filename preferences stay in local extension storage until you clear them or uninstall BVT.</li>
        <li>The profile <code>secUid</code> cache is a small recent mapping. Older entries are trimmed as new profiles are seen.</li>
        <li>The Pro credential stays until you sign out, clear it, or uninstall the extension.</li>
        <li>Downloaded files are written to your browser’s download location or a folder you choose. They remain under your control.</li>
        <li>BVT does not keep a server-side copy of your downloads or page data.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>7. This website</h2>
      <p>
        This website is a static site. It does not load a tag manager, advertising pixels,
        embedded videos, third-party fonts, or a contact form. It does not set its own
        cookies. The hosting provider may process standard request metadata such as IP
        address, user agent, and timestamp for delivery, security, and abuse prevention
        under its own policy.
      </p>

      {
        gaEnabled ? (
          <>
            <h3>Google Analytics (enabled on this build)</h3>
            <p>
              This build uses Google Analytics 4 with measurement ID{' '}
              <code>{SITE.gaMeasurementId}</code>. GA4 may collect page views, approximate
              location derived from the request, device and browser information, and
              interaction events, and may set <code>_ga</code> cookies. BVT uses this only
              to understand aggregate website usage. The extension itself does not contain
              Google Analytics.
            </p>
          </>
        ) : (
          <>
            <h3>Google Analytics (not enabled on this build)</h3>
            <p>
              No Google Analytics measurement ID is configured for this build, so no GA tag
              is rendered. If a measurement ID is later configured at build time, this
              section and the site’s script loading will change together.
            </p>
          </>
        )
      }

      <h2>8. Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This website does not set its own cookies. If Google Analytics is enabled for a
        build, GA may set its own cookies as described above. The extension uses extension
        storage, not website cookies, for its settings.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Third parties</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>TikTok</strong> — the public pages you open and the media or page endpoints the extension requests at your direction.</li>
        <li><strong>Chrome Web Store</strong> — distribution and installation. Its own policies apply.</li>
        <li><strong>pandahi.cc</strong> — Pro checkout and license validation.</li>
        <li><strong>Static hosting provider</strong> — website delivery and standard request logs.</li>
        <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> — only when enabled for the website build.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        BVT does not sell page data. It does not share page data with the subscription
        server. It does not provide a server-side download or storage service.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Clear extension settings and local data from the extension or Chrome’s extension settings.</li>
        <li>Uninstall the extension to remove its local extension storage.</li>
        <li>Close the page to clear the in-memory panel state.</li>
        <li>Choose your own download folder, or cancel a download before it completes.</li>
        <li>Disable or delete cookies in your browser if GA is enabled for a build.</li>
        <li>Contact support with a privacy question.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>11. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For privacy questions or support, email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`} class="font-semibold">
          {SITE.supportEmail}
        </a>
        . Do not send account credentials, page data, or subscription tokens in a support
        request.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        This policy may change as the extension and website evolve. The "Last updated" date
        at the top will change when it does. Material changes should be reviewed before the
        next public release.
      </p>

      <div class="not-prose mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-5 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">
        <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Independent product</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          BVT is an independent browser extension and is not affiliated with, endorsed by,
          or sponsored by TikTok or ByteDance. TikTok and related marks are trademarks of
          their respective owners.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
